OneiOS (port/oruma-2026-11-24, 2026-11-25): the switch of the Adreno shader fixes 0101 and 0102 (on by default since 2026-11-25).

METAL2VULKAN_SHADER_FIX=1 (read once per process, env_vars::shader_fix; the Metal plug-in sets it unless the boot
argument oneios-m2v-shader-fix=0, userland/metal/ShaderFix.inc) turns on 0101's rule (a run-time-indexed constant
table past 4 KiB read from the constant blob) and 0102's cast and GEP arms of blob_const_offset. Off, both are the
pin's code paths: the same translations, and the device profile's fingerprint is the pin's, so the shader cache's
entries stay valid. On, the fingerprint takes the switch, so translations made with and without it never meet in
the cache (metal2vulkan-runtime's shader cache keys an entry on the profile fingerprint). Applied after 0101 and 0102.

diff --git a/crates/metal2vulkan/src/device/profile.rs b/crates/metal2vulkan/src/device/profile.rs
index 5c5d8c3..ec466a0 100644
--- a/crates/metal2vulkan/src/device/profile.rs
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan/src/device/profile.rs
@@ -438,6 +438,11 @@ fn fingerprint_of(fields: &ProfileFields) -> Hash256 {
     note_fingerprint_derived();
     let mut h = Hashing(Sha256::new());
     h.0.update(b"metal2vulkan/device-profile/v1\0");
+    // OneiOS: the shader fix (env_vars::shader_fix) changes what is compiled; hashed only when on,
+    // so the fingerprint without it is the pin's and translations made with and without it never meet.
+    if crate::env_vars::shader_fix() {
+        h.0.update(b"oneios-shader-fix-0101-0102\0");
+    }
     // `Hashing` never fails, and `Debug` of these plain-data types only fails when the
     // writer does.
     let _ = write!(h, "{:?}", fields);
